  "knowledgeItems": [
    {
      "id": "kb-1",
      "title": "Cloud Migration Best Practices",
      "type": "guide",
      "category": "Cloud",
      "tags": ["cloud", "migration", "aws", "azure"],
      "description": "Comprehensive guide for planning and executing cloud migrations",
      "markdownContent": "# Cloud Migration Best Practices\n\n## Pre-Migration Phase\n\n1. **Assessment**\n   - Inventory all applications and dependencies\n   - Identify migration candidates\n   - Assess technical debt\n\n2. **Planning**\n   - Define migration strategy (6 Rs)\n   - Create migration roadmap\n   - Establish success criteria\n\n## Migration Strategies\n\n- **Rehost**: Lift-and-shift\n- **Replatform**: Lift, tinker, and shift\n- **Refactor**: Re-architect for cloud-native\n- **Retire**: Decommission\n- **Retain**: Keep on-premises\n- **Repurchase**: Move to SaaS\n\n## Best Practices\n\n- Start with non-critical workloads\n- Automate where possible\n- Test thoroughly\n- Monitor continuously\n- Document everything",
      "author": "John Anderson",
      "lastUpdated": "2024-03-10T10:00:00Z",
      "viewCount": 145,
      "region": "Global"
    },
    {
      "id": "kb-2",
      "title": "Kubernetes Cluster Setup SOP",
      "type": "sop",
      "category": "Platform",
      "tags": ["kubernetes", "devops", "containers"],
      "description": "Standard operating procedure for setting up production Kubernetes clusters",
      "contentUrl": "https://portal.example.com/docs/k8s-setup-sop.pdf",
