      "id": "kb-5",
      "title": "AI/ML Model Deployment Guide",
      "type": "documentation",
      "category": "AI/ML",
      "tags": ["ai", "ml", "deployment", "mlops"],
      "description": "Guide for deploying and monitoring ML models in production",
      "markdownContent": "# AI/ML Model Deployment Guide\n\n## Overview\n\nThis guide covers best practices for deploying machine learning models to production.\n\n## Deployment Options\n\n### 1. Batch Inference\n- Scheduled predictions\n- Large dataset processing\n- Lower latency requirements\n\n### 2. Real-time Inference\n- API endpoints\n- Low latency required\n- Individual predictions\n\n### 3. Edge Deployment\n- On-device inference\n- Offline capability\n- Privacy-focused\n\n## MLOps Pipeline\n\n1. **Model Training**\n   - Version training data\n   - Track experiments\n   - Save model artifacts\n\n2. **Model Validation**\n   - Test on holdout set\n   - A/B testing\n   - Shadow mode deployment\n\n3. **Model Serving**\n   - Containerize models\n   - Load balancing\n   - Auto-scaling\n\n4. **Monitoring**\n   - Track model performance\n   - Monitor data drift\n   - Alert on anomalies\n\n## Tools\n\n- MLflow for experiment tracking\n- Kubernetes for orchestration\n- Prometheus for monitoring\n- Grafana for visualization",
      "author": "Sarah Chen",
      "lastUpdated": "2024-03-12T15:00:00Z",
      "viewCount": 132,
      "region": "Global"
